WEBVTT

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.730
Teruto Kurabe gets the first move.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.400
It's starting.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.320
Yeah.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.820
This is the final battle.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.740
Does this mean I finally get to see my dream?

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.200
Call. Margreia.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.080
Call. Bloom.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.130
Teruto.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.840
I'm going to smash you to smithereens.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.180
Kikka.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.510
I...

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:38.800
Ready?

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.810
Build-Divide.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.480
#11 Heads or Tails

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.540
Where am I?

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.550
Welcome back, Teruto Kurabe.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:37.760
Who are you?

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.140
<i>The battle against the King. Rebuild.</i>

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:45.060
<i>Three years ago, I took part in that battle.</i>

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.680
<i>However, after I defeated the King...</i>

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.440
<i>When I opened my eyes, I saw...</i>

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.230
Where am I?

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.230
This is Kyoto.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:59.150
Kyoto? Not Neo Kyoto?

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.910
Your wish was granted, and an exception
was made for you to be brought back here.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.950
Brought back?

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.270
Hey. What is this blue stuff?

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.820
<i>It was like a dream, this world.</i>

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.740
<i>This world with an "outside"
stretching as far as the eye could see.</i>

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.700
Using Bloom to attack the player.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.880
Winner. Teruto Kurabe.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.500
Yes! Undefeated.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.510
Aren't there any better players out there?

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:08.640
Hey.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.560
I've been here for about two years now.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.940
I've done nothing but play Build-Divide every day.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.270
Are you sure I should just be playing like this?

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:21.990
It is fine. It is also my Master's wish that
you continue to play Build-Divide.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:27.320
Really? Who knew this world would be such
a cakewalk after defeating the King?

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.950
Hey, how about introducing me
to this Master guy soon?

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.870
I mean, I'd like to thank him for bringing me here.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.040
His location is not far from here.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.290
Really?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.260
<i>Then, the day came.</i>

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.520
Teruto, my Master will see you now.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:53.810
This way, please.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.060
Right.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.110
Isn't this...

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.280
...a bit much?

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.950
Are you going to dissect me or something?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.570
Neither near...

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.370
...nor far, I suppose.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.450
Who are you?

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:17.580
I am the Master of this realm, Mario Higuma.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.920
Mario Higuma?

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.840
I lost my physical body many years ago.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.300
My consciousness has been digitized.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.260
Really? Wow.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:31.260
I've observed your battles.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:34.140
Here in this world, and in Neo Kyoto.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:34.890
Huh?

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.100
Your battle against the King was especially amazing.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:43.190
Ever since the Neo Kyoto System was built,
you've had the highest magical power aptitude.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.240
Your power is beyond satisfactory.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.530
Therefore, I have chosen you.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.320
Huh? For what?

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:57.540
Teruto Kurabe. With your talent for Build-Divide,
you will become my vessel.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.580
Vessel?

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:03.420
I mean to overwrite my mind into that body of yours.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.090
I'm headed off to make my own preparations.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.760
I leave the rest to you.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.680
H-Hey!

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.010
Now then, Teruto. This way, please.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:14.720
What the hell? Stay away.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.230
Get out of my way!

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:44.670
I don't get it.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.010
They said they brought me here to grant my wish.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.470
Overwriting my mind, becoming a vessel.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:54.890
I have to get out of here.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.360
Where's the exit?

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.740
NEO KYOTO

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.370
Neo Kyoto...

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.170
Is this...

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:33.140
...where I ended up after battling the King?

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.690
May I help you with something?

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:45.690
Crap.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.070
Starting the scan.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.530
Verification complete.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.660
Confirmed that you are Teruto Kurabe.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.740
Nice to meet you.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:59.040
I am Neo Kyoto System's guardian, Rimp.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.080
Is something the matter?

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.040
Are you different from the others?

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.380
What do you mean by "others"?

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.960
I need to ask you. What is this place?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.220
This is the main server of Neo Kyoto.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:16.550
Main server? Like a lifeline?

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:22.600
No. The Neo Kyoto System operates
within this server. It is run in here.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.940
System? Operates?

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:29.900
The Neo Kyoto System is a virtual city system
developed by the Billmon company.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:33.110
We connect to our citizens through
those barrels over there.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.320
We convert their minds into signals,
and transmit them to the virtual city.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:40.660
We have everyone connected in
parallel to this brain structure,

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:46.330
and use them as additional memory
for the server's calculations.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:55.050
This is how everyone is able to lead
their lives in the virtual city while asleep.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:09:00.760
This is how the virtual city of Neo Kyoto works,
developed by Master Higuma.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:06.270
No way. You're saying the city
I've always lived in isn't even real?

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:10.020
Just as your mind is genuine,
you could say the city is real.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.400
It's just that, what you live in is a virtual city.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.030
What are you saying? I just don't understand.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.120
Then, allow me to explain again.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.780
I don't want you to explain.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:24.080
This just means that Neo Kyoto is a fake city.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.250
No, it is real.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.790
Our citizens all live in Neo Kyoto.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:38.260
You, your family, and your friends are all
connected to this server and live in this virtual city.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:39.930
What the...

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:43.850
Me too?

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:50.400
Why would he create a system like this?

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:55.280
I can't accept it, that I've been living in a virtual city.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:59.370
A world like this can only end up
breaking and ceasing to exist.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.330
There is nothing to worry about.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.910
Among the lifeforms connected to our barrels,

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:10.380
we've placed those with exceptional talent
for Build-Divide onto the main CPU.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:15.340
They are fused with our program
to ensure stable operation of the city.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:19.640
Although these lifeforms will be
depleted at a rapid pace,

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:24.430
we can avoid glitches and bugs
thanks to their computational power.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:29.810
Currently, we have the best
lifeform of all time connected.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.940
So in our eyes,
it's impossible for any problems to occur.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.110
Then, the King is actually...

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:40.450
The lifeform set as the main CPU,
as well as the program itself.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:49.040
Up to now, there have been many lifeforms
set as the main CPU for Neo Kyoto.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:54.800
Without them, we would not have
been able to continue running Neo Kyoto.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.340
In order to maintain Neo Kyoto,

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:01.720
we must continue to keep the most powerful
and highest competence Build-Divide player

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:04.510
connected to our CPU.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:10.100
Therefore, the battles that show us
who has the most talent are...

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.900
Rebuilds, right?

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.130
Kikka...

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:37.510
Kikka?

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.930
What are you doing here?

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.260
After your battle against the King,

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:50.060
we did not replace the lifeform
fused with the program,

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.650
so we held another Rebuild.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:57.190
She was the one who defeated the King
and then rose to the top.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:58.480
Why?

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.990
I have no doubts.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.280
Kikka has always been chasing after me.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:10.370
She must have been looking for me
when she challenged the King.

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:15.420
Battling the King is validation
of one's Build-Divide skills.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:20.050
Every time we need to exchange the CPU
due to its impending expiration,

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:23.430
we search for competent players,
and set whoever manages to reach the King,

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.890
regardless of whether they win or lose,
as the next CPU.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:31.600
Then we update the program,
therefore maintaining Neo Kyoto.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:34.520
I ended up here even though I battled the King.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.360
That is because you were chosen by my Master.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.530
You lied about granting our wishes.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:45.070
No matter what, anyone who
challenges the King is doomed to be captured.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.240
Play with me, Teruto.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.830
Is something the matter?

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.830
Kikka.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:01.960
I'm going.

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:03.630
One more time.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.720
To Neo Kyoto.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:11.970
Forced connection.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:13.730
System error.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.560
Due to decreased load on his memory,

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:19.570
Teruto Kurabe's memory data
will be partially deleted.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:22.280
To think that you'd return of your own volition.

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.610
Because we used an old barrel,

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:30.030
forcing his removal could cause
a serious error with Teruto Kurabe.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:31.790
What should we do?

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.370
It doesn't matter.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:37.290
His and Kikka's powers are immeasurable.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:43.340
If we can combine them,
they might lead the King to greater heights.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.930
Should that happen, my wish...

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.220
Teruto Kurabe.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.390
Battle.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.010
With the King.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.610
Where am I?

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.960
Using Viena to attack the player.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.290
Using Grona to attack Viena.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:24.460
Using Ambition Eater to attack the player.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:29.930
End of turn.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:34.010
Nice. With the additional damage,
now it's ten to seven.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:38.640
The match just started, but the air feels heavy.

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:40.310
Sakura.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:43.690
They're resonating with each other.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:47.650
Together, they're even more than I imagined.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:51.780
Show me more. Release more power.

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:53.280
My turn.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:55.450
I'm going to use Grona. Accept.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.960
Attacking Ambition Eater.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.250
I can attack Teruto now.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:07.380
Using the other Grona to attack his Territory.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.600
Burst again?

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:16.970
They're even on lives now.

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:19.140
Back to square one, huh?

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:22.230
Excuse me, whose side are you on?

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:24.570
Are you rooting for Kikka?

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:29.490
I only want one thing.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:30.110
Huh?

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:33.910
I wonder if I'll get my hands on it this time.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.710
Now we're even, seven to seven.

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:43.670
I'm so happy.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:46.550
You only have eyes for me, Teruto.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.760
I've waited for this moment for so long.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:53.550
Keep looking only at me, Teruto.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:55.970
My turn.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.140
Here I go.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:05.110
Kikka.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.990
Sending all living beings into chaos.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.860
Repeating death and rebirth.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:15.370
Accept.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.330
Bloom, Soul Wager.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:24.540
Territory. Build Arise.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.930
Tower of Trials.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.050
This Territory...

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.810
It's not Casino of Fate.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:42.060
What's this? A wardrobe change?

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.690
I'm thrilled.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.900
You obtained it just for me?

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:49.690
Show me, Teruto. This Territory's power.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:52.110
Activating Tower of Trials' ability.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.110
Revealing the top two cards of my deck.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.950
Adding Bertruga, Black Sword Dragon to my hand.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.120
The other goes to the Cemetery.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.410
Amazing, this Territory.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:05.420
He added to his hand while increasing
his Cemetery to seven cards.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.420
Activating Bloom's ability.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.090
Accept.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:11.920
Rizome, Black Knight.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:14.720
Using Rizome to attack Grona.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:21.020
You're trying so hard just for me.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.230
I've got to live up to that. Draw.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.570
Putting everything in the universe on a scale.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.570
Thou who brings judgment upon others.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:34.110
Accept.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:37.530
Margreia, Angel of Justice.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.830
Territory. Build Arise.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.090
Shrine of Justice.

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:58.590
This is Kikka's new Territory.

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.430
The one Sakura took down.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.310
Activating Epitaph of Conviction's ability.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.770
Increasing all units with three thousand power.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:09.440
Using Margreia to attack Rizome.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.200
You can wave goodbye to your decoy now.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:17.950
Next, using Grona to attack.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:20.320
Disappear, Bloom.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.040
Activating Bloom's ability.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:27.710
During my opponent's turn, I'm sending
the top card of my deck to the Cemetery.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.830
Yay! Buster Card.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.670
Increasing Bloom's power by five thousand.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:40.930
Too bad. I really wanted Bloom to disappear.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.680
Seems I was unlucky there.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.850
Okay, just bring it on as much as you want.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:51.150
Every time you rise up,
I'll just enjoy crushing you again.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:56.110
Really, Kikka. You seem to be
enjoying yourself more than usual.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:59.320
All right, Teruto. Let's see you struggle.

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:01.530
All the way to hell.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:06.000
My turn. Draw.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:09.330
Activating Tower of Trials' ability.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:11.830
Revealing the top two cards of my deck.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.750
Sending Rizome to my hand.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.250
Sending the other to the Cemetery.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.800
Accept. Mantis, Witch of the Death Dance.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:21.970
Activating Mantis' ability.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:23.760
Discarding one card from my hand.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:26.720
Come back to life. Aria of Bloody Revenge.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:28.310
Attacking Margreia.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:35.730
Now, using Mantis to launch
a Two-Hit Attack on the player.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:42.030
Burst. Additional damage.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.700
Burst again. One more.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:48.700
No way.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:51.920
Shot Trigger. Angelic Order.

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.460
Consuming two Conviction Counters.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:58.010
If the top card of my deck is a Judgment unit,
I'm sending it to the field.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:19:59.800
That's...

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:03.430
Elizabelt, Angel of Law.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.180
Activating Elizabelt's ability.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:09.850
Consuming one Conviction Counter
and drawing one card.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.770
Then, Margreia. Accept.

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:16.360
He got her down to three lives,
but now she has all her units lined up.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:17.730
Master.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:20.950
Aria returns to the Cemetery during the end phase.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:26.580
I really love playing Build-Divide with you.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:33.580
I wish I could savor this time forever,
but all things must come to an end.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:38.800
Sorry, but this will be my last battle with you.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:44.220
When this showdown ends,
I'm locking you inside me.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:51.480
Don't worry. Even if you cease to exist,
I won't miss you.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.150
You'll go on living inside me forever.

00:20:56.310 --> 00:21:01.190
Then we're going to play forever. You and me.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:05.700
Since that's my sole wish.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:09.330
Activating Epitaph of Conviction's ability.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.790
Revealing the top card of my deck.

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:14.290
Adding Helmina, Angel of Oblivion to my hand.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:15.580
Accept.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.420
Elizabelt, Angel of Law.

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:20.750
Activating Elizabelt's ability.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:23.220
Drawing one card.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:27.470
Then from my hand,
Helmina, Angel of Oblivion. Accept.

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:28.720
Activating her ability.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.810
Nullifying Bloom's ability with this turn.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:32.980
What?

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:36.150
Then, even if he sends her to block,
she'll be destroyed right away.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:39.320
If Bloom gets taken down now...

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:41.900
This is payback for your last turn.

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:44.490
Starting with you. Mantis.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:46.910
Using Margreia to attack.

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:52.040
You're next, Teruto.

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.580
Using Elizabelt to launch a Two-Hit Attack.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:00.290
Then, using the other Elizabelt
to launch a Two-Hit Attack.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:09.600
Five lives at once?

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:13.680
I'm not done. Using Helmina to attack Teruto.

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:22.150
You're down to one life, Teruto.

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:24.360
No way.

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:25.690
She turned the tables.

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:32.280
How about it? Can you still turn it around?

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:33.990
All you've done before is lose.

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:37.330
There's no way you can defeat me, right?

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:41.000
Kikka.

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:47.420
When I came back to Neo Kyoto, I hated the King.

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:51.180
I was certain that it was hatred for you.

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:56.310
The thing is though, I don't hate you at all.

00:22:57.600 --> 00:23:01.150
I didn't come back here to defeat you.

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:07.950
Kikka. I...

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:23.420
I came here...

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:25.590
...to tell you I'm sorry.

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:29.970
TO BE CONTINUED

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:32.300
What do you mean, you're sorry?

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:36.810
Sakura, please help Master.

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:39.980
#12 End of the Road

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:39.440
I'm going to trust the path I take.
